The NoSuchMethodError in your processAsync method is a classic **Library Version Conflict**. This happens when the code is compiled against one version of a library (like Apache POI) but finds a different version at runtime that is missing a specific method [cite: 20-21, 530-533].
### The Root Cause: Apache POI Version Mismatch
The most common cause for this error in your current code is the usage of **CellType** or the **StreamingReader** library I suggested earlier.
 1. **CellType Changes:** In Apache POI 4.0+, getCellType() changed from returning an int to returning an Enum. [cite_start]If your pom.xml has mixed versions (e.g., poi is 5.2.0 but poi-ooxml is 3.17), the code crashes because the method signatures don't match.
 2. **StreamingReader Conflict:** If you implemented the com.monitorjbl.xlsx.StreamingReader logic I provided, that library is known to crash with NoSuchMethodError when used with **POI 5.x** because it looks for methods that were removed in the newer POI versions.
### The Fix: Standard POI "Safe" Streaming
To handle 500,000 records **without** external libraries that cause version errors, use the native **XSSFReader** with a **XSSFSheetXMLHandler**. [cite_start]This is built into standard POI and is the most memory-efficient way to read Excel files [cite: 581-582].
**Replace your parseExcelStream and parseSheet methods with this version:**
```java
// Add these imports at the top
import org.apache.poi.openxml4j.opc.OPCPackage;
import org.apache.poi.xssf.eventusermodel.ReadOnlySharedStringsTable;
import org.apache.poi.xssf.eventusermodel.XSSFReader;
import org.apache.poi.xssf.eventusermodel.XSSFSheetXMLHandler;
import org.apache.poi.xssf.model.StylesTable;
import org.xml.sax.InputSource;
import org.xml.sax.XMLReader;
import org.apache.poi.util.XMLHelper;

private ParsingResult parseExcelStream(InputStream is, LocalDate postingDate) throws IOException {
    List<ExcelRowData> list = new ArrayList<>();
    // Using a boolean array so it can be modified inside the inner class
    final boolean[] hasProductCol = {false};

    try {
        OPCPackage pkg = OPCPackage.open(is);
        ReadOnlySharedStringsTable strings = new ReadOnlySharedStringsTable(pkg);
        XSSFReader xssfReader = new XSSFReader(pkg);
        StylesTable styles = xssfReader.getStylesTable();
        XSSFReader.SheetIterator iter = (XSSFReader.SheetIterator) xssfReader.getSheetsData();

        if (iter.hasNext()) {
            try (InputStream sheetStream = iter.next()) {
                InputSource sheetSource = new InputSource(sheetStream);
                XMLReader sheetParser = XMLHelper.newXMLReader();
                
                // This handler processes the XML row-by-row without loading everything to RAM
                XSSFSheetXMLHandler handler = new XXSSFSheetXMLHandler(styles, strings, new XXSSFSheetXMLHandler.SheetContentsHandler() {
                    private ExcelRowData currentRow;

                    @Override
                    public void startRow(int rowNum) {
                        currentRow = new ExcelRowData();
                        currentRow.rowIndex = rowNum;
                    }

                    @Override
                    public void endRow(int rowNum) {
                        if (currentRow != null && !isEmpty(currentRow)) {
                            list.add(currentRow);
                        }
                    }

                    @Override
                    public void cell(String cellRef, String formattedValue, Comment comment) {
                        int colIdx = new org.apache.poi.ss.util.CellReference(cellRef).getCol();
                        applyBusinessLogic(currentRow, colIdx, formattedValue, hasProductCol, postingDate);
                    }
                }, false);
                
                sheetParser.setContentHandler(handler);
                sheetParser.parse(sheetSource);
            }
        }
        pkg.close();
    } catch (Exception e) {
        log.error("EXCEL_EVENT_PARSE_FAIL | Reason: {}", e.getMessage());
        throw new IOException("Failed to parse Excel using Event API", e);
    }
    return new ParsingResult(list, hasProductCol[0]);
}

/**
 * RE-INTEGRATED BUSINESS LOGIC
 * This ensures your "01" vs Standard logic is 100% preserved.
 */
private void applyBusinessLogic(ExcelRowData d, int col, String val, boolean[] hasProduct, LocalDate postingDate) {
    if (val == null) return;
    String cleanVal = val.trim();

    [cite_start]// Preserve your "01" System Format Logic [cite: 586-591]
    if (col == 0) {
        d.sysSite = cleanVal;
        if ("01".equals(cleanVal)) d.isSystemFormat = true;
    }

    if (d.isSystemFormat) {
        switch (col) {
            case 1 -> d.sysDate = cleanVal;
            case 2 -> d.sysYear = cleanVal;
            case 3 -> d.sysPeriod = cleanVal;
            case 4 -> d.branch = cleanVal;
            case 5 -> d.currency = cleanVal.toUpperCase();
            case 6 -> d.cgl = cleanVal;
            case 7 -> { /* Handled in endRow or via a temp amount holder */ }
            case 9 -> d.remarks = cleanVal;
            case 10 -> {
                d.productCode = cleanVal;
                if (!cleanVal.isEmpty() && !"A".equalsIgnoreCase(cleanVal)) hasProduct[0] = true;
            }
        }
    } else {
        [cite_start]// Standard Format Logic [cite: 592-596]
        switch (col) {
            case 0 -> d.branch = cleanVal;
            case 1 -> d.currency = cleanVal.toUpperCase();
            case 2 -> d.cgl = cleanVal;
            case 5 -> d.remarks = cleanVal;
            case 6 -> {
                d.productCode = cleanVal;
                if (!cleanVal.isEmpty() && !"A".equalsIgnoreCase(cleanVal)) hasProduct[0] = true;
            }
        }
    }
}

private boolean isEmpty(ExcelRowData d) {
    return (d.branch == null || d.branch.isEmpty()) && (d.cgl == null || d.cgl.isEmpty());
}

